# 1-based lines to bookmark. Each sits INSIDE a construct the profile claims to
# understand, so a broken `containers` shows up as a missing breadcrumb.
#
# Switch arms and if-branches are given different shapes on purpose: identical
# sibling statements make the generated structural query ambiguous and codemark
# refuses the bookmark. That's a sample-authoring constraint, not a profile
# defect.

# Inside the constructor's guard clause — constructor > class > namespace.
83

# Inside a switch arm inside the foreach inside Compute(). The deepest chain in
# the file: namespace > class > method > foreach > switch > arm. `switch_body`
# and `switch_section` are deliberately unlabelled wrappers, so the breadcrumb
# names the method rather than the branch.
#
# This targets the arm's `var taxed` declaration rather than the `Total +=`
# below it. Because `switch_section` is (correctly) not a landmark, the query
# has no anchor inside the arm, so `Total += taxed;` is indistinguishable from
# `Total -= amount;` in Pay() — two compound assignments to the same field in
# the same class. A uniquely shaped declaration gives the query something to
# match on. Same class of limitation as codemark#239.
131

# Inside the local function declared in Compute()'s body — proves
# `local_function_statement` works as a container, which only idiomatic code
# reaches (a parser corpus has no reason to nest one).
147

# Inside the LINQ chain in SettleAsync(), an async method.
158

# Inside the catch filter in Pay().
190

# Inside Render() in the nested `class Summary` — proves type-in-type
# containment: namespace > class > class > method.
218

# Inside Register() on the generic `InvoiceBook<TInvoice>`, which is outside
# the Invoice class entirely.
234

# Inside TryFind() on the same generic class.
239

# NOT bookmarkable, recorded rather than silently omitted:
#
#   104    get => total;
#   105    private set
#
# An `accessor_declaration` has no `name` field, so the generator emits an
# impossible `name:` pattern for the enclosing property and tree-sitter rejects
# the query. Reproduces with an empty profile, so no curation can fix it. This
# is codemark#239 — the same root cause as the Lua case.
